# Cypress E2E Testing Guide

- Tests live under [`tests/cypress`](mdc:tests/cypress). Run via your local Cypress setup.
- Use existing helpers under `tests/cypress/support` to reduce duplication.
- Prefer data-testid or stable selectors; avoid brittle class-based selectors from built assets.
- For complex UI flows, structure tests by feature directory and co-locate fixtures.
- Keep tests idempotent and independent; reset state explicitly when needed.

## CI/Local

- Refer to `tests/cypress/readme.md` for environment details and splitting via `cypress-split.js`.